}

\AuthorResponse{
We agree that the previous comparison did not constitute a formal usability study. Because a formal usability evaluation could not be completed within this revision cycle, the revised manuscript no longer claims that DentalClaw has been demonstrated to reduce the technical barrier for dentists or researchers.

Instead, all related statements have been reframed as design intent (``is designed to reduce the coordination burden of multi-step dental AI experiments''), the manually operated comparison is explicitly reported as a workflow demonstration rather than a controlled human-factor experiment, and the absence of a formal usability experiment is listed as a limitation with user-facing validation identified as necessary future work.

